{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,24]],"date-time":"2026-08-24T01:48:26Z","timestamp":1787536106288,"version":"build-2736575974"},"reference-count":105,"publisher":"Copernicus GmbH","issue":"1","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,2]],"date-time":"2024-01-02T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1704153600000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/100000001","name":"National Science Foundation","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["AGS-1649212"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["AGS-1649212"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100000001","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/100000001","name":"National Science Foundation","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["AGS-2220307"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["AGS-2220307"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100000001","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/100006488","name":"Division of Agriculture and Natural Resources, University of California","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["CA-D-LAW-6403-RR"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["CA-D-LAW-6403-RR"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100006488","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/100006488","name":"Division of Agriculture and Natural Resources, University of California","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["CA-D-ETX-2102-H"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["CA-D-ETX-2102-H"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100006488","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/100007707","name":"University of California, Davis","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["Donald G. Crosby Graduate Fellowships in Environmental Chemistry and Jastro-Shields Research Awards"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["Donald G. Crosby Graduate Fellowships in Environmental Chemistry and Jastro-Shields Research Awards"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100007707","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Atmos. Chem. Phys."],"abstract":"<jats:p>Abstract. Fog\/cloud drops and aerosol liquid water are important sites for the transformations of atmospheric species, largely through reactions with photoformed oxidants such as the hydroxyl radical (\u26abOH), singlet molecular oxygen (1O2\u2217), and oxidizing triplet excited states of organic matter (3C\u2217). Despite their importance, few studies have measured these oxidants or their seasonal variations. To address this gap, we collected ambient PM2.5 from Davis, California, over the course of a year and measured photooxidant concentrations and light absorption in dilute aqueous extracts. Mass absorption coefficients (MACs) normalized by dissolved organic carbon range from 0.4\u20133.8\u2009m2 per gram\u2009C at 300\u2009nm. Concentrations of \u26abOH, 1O2\u2217, and 3C\u2217 in the extracts range from (0.2\u20134.7)\u2009\u00d7\u200910\u221215\u2009M, (0.7\u201345)\u2009\u00d7\u200910\u221213\u2009M, and (0.03\u20137.9)\u2009\u00d7\u200910\u221213\u2009M, respectively, with biomass burning brown carbon playing a major role in light absorption and the formation of 1O2\u2217 and 3C\u2217. Extrapolating photooxidant kinetics from our dilute particle extracts to concentrated aerosol liquid water (ALW) conditions gives an estimated \u26abOH concentration of 7\u2009\u00d7\u200910\u221215\u2009M and ranges for 1O2\u2217 and 3C\u2217 of (0.6\u20137)\u2009\u00d7\u200910\u221212\u2009M and (0.2\u20131)\u2009\u00d7\u200910\u221212\u2009M, respectively. Compared to the results in Kaur et\u00a0al. (2019), our ALW predictions show roughly 10\u00a0times higher \u26abOH, up to 5\u00a0times higher 3C, and 1O2\u2217 concentrations that are lower by factors of 20\u2013100. These concentrations suggest that 3C\u2217 and 1O2\u2217 in ALW dominate the processing of organic compounds that react quickly with these oxidants (e.g., phenols and furans, respectively), while \u26abOH is more important for less reactive organics.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.5194\/acp-24-1-2024","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,2]],"date-time":"2024-01-02T06:32:59Z","timestamp":1704177179000},"page":"1-21","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":19,"title":["Seasonal variations in photooxidant formation and light absorption in aqueous extracts of ambient particles"],"prefix":"10.5194","volume":"24","author":[{"given":"Lan","family":"Ma","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Reed","family":"Worland","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Laura","family":"Heinlein","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Chrystal","family":"Guzman","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Wenqing","family":"Jiang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Christopher","family":"Niedek","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-4865-2951","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Keith J.","family":"Bein","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-5203-8778","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Qi","family":"Zhang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-3020-7024","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Cort","family":"Anastasio","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"3145","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,2]]},"reference":[{"key":"ref1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Alfarra, M. R., Prevot, A. S. H., Szidat, S., Sandradewi, J., Weimer, S., Lanz, V. A., Schreiber, D., Mohr, M., and Baltensperger, U.: Identification of the Mass Spectral Signature of Organic Aerosols from Wood Burning Emissions, Environ. Sci. Technol., 41, 5770\u20135777, https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1021\/es062289b, 2007.","DOI":"10.1021\/es062289b"},{"key":"ref2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Anastasio, C. and McGregor, K. G.: Chemistry of fog waters in California's Central Valley: 1.\u00a0In situ photoformation of hydroxyl radical and singlet molecular oxygen, Atmos. Environ., 35, 1079\u20131089, https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/S1352-2310(00)00281-8, 2001.","DOI":"10.1016\/S1352-2310(00)00281-8"},{"key":"ref3","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Appiani, E., Ossola, R., Latch, D. E., Erickson, P. R., and McNeill, K.: Aqueous singlet oxygen reaction kinetics of furfuryl alcohol: effect of temperature, pH, and salt content, Environ. Sci.-Proc. Imp., 19, 507\u2013516, https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1039\/C6EM00646A, 2017.","DOI":"10.1039\/C6EM00646A"},{"key":"ref4","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Arakaki, T., Anastasio, C., Kuroki, Y., Nakajima, H., Okada, K., Kotani, Y., Handa, D., Azechi, S., Kimura, T., Tsuhako, A., and Miyagi, Y.: A general scavenging rate constant for reaction of hydroxyl radical with organic carbon in atmospheric waters, Environ. Sci. Technol., 47, 8196\u20138203, https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1021\/es401927b, 2013.","DOI":"10.1021\/es401927b"},{"key":"ref5","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Ashton, L., Buxton, G. V., and Stuart, C. R.: Temperature dependence of the rate of reaction of OH with some aromatic compounds in aqueous solution. Evidence for the formation of a \u03c0-complex intermediate?, J.\u00a0Chem. Soc. Faraday\u00a0T., 91, 1631\u20131633, https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1039\/FT9959101631, 1995.","DOI":"10.1039\/FT9959101631"},{"key":"ref6","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Baba, Y., Yatagai, T., Harada, T., a